From b36b8703ff505b67c27fb3faf4a6162bba5aca43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Steiner <tomac@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:11:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] [iOS] Back the built-in AI APIs with on-device models

Exposes the Prompt API (`LanguageModel`) and the Summarizer, Writer,
Rewriter, Translator, and LanguageDetector APIs to web pages in
WebKit-based Chrome for iOS, behind the `ios-built-in-ai-apis` flag.

The APIs come from the prompt-api-polyfill and the built-in AI task API
polyfills, injected into every frame at document start in the page
content world. Their `native` backend talks over a script message
handler to `BuiltInAIEngine`, which runs the models:

- Apple Foundation Models where the device has Apple Intelligence, for
  text on iOS 26 and for images on iOS 27.
- Gemma 4 E2B through LiteRT-LM otherwise, and for audio. The model is
  downloaded once into the app container and shared by every origin.
  It runs on the GPU on devices with 6 GB of RAM or more, and on the
  CPU on 4 GB devices.

LiteRT-LM is fetched by third_party/litert_lm/fetch.py and built when
`enable_litert_lm` is set. `ios_chrome_minimal_entitlements` signs
Chrome with entitlements that an App ID provisioned through the App
Store Connect API can grant.
